                        "entry_id": "5338f7f8-fa38-3412-b5b6-6c1ab8813da0",
                        "glosses": [
                            "In Blanchard's transsexualism typology, the supposed paraphilic tendency of a male person to be sexually aroused by the thought of being a female, sometimes framed as a form of gender identity disorder or transvestic fetishism."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "uncountable"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "cb93c097-0f60-4086-8e6a-b74c707db62d",
                                "sense_id": "6136b746-b389-3cf7-8cc9-f6f7ffc18314",
                                "text": "Charles Moser (2010), “Blanchard’s Autogynephilia Theory: A Critique”, in Journal of Homosexuality, volume 57, number 6, →DOI, pages 790–809: “If autogynephilia were a paraphilia, we would expect that MTFs would want estrogens to feminize themselves, but decline anti-androgens or report that they disliked the effect. This is contrary to the observation that MTFs request and like the effects of anti-androgens.”"
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
